NOTICE — kovan-web
==================

Licence: AGPL-3.0-only (from its creation, 2026-10-06)
------------------------------------------------------

kovan-web is web-kovan, the Code Review UI of the kovan family (GitHub
#736). ~~The maintainer directed that it be AGPL-3.0-only "since it is part of
the kovan family"~~ **CORRECTED 2026-10-06:** AGPL-3.0-only was set by the
session's brief to the building agent ("like the kovan family"), not by a
maintainer direction. **Confirmed AGPL-3.0-only by the maintainer the same
day:** "I thought kovan web needed pdf reader that's why I did AGPLv3".
web-kovan is to open literature PDFs in kovan's own reader, fetched from the
corpus repository's raw GitHub URL (decided on #729), which means carrying
`kopitiam-pdf`, MuPDF-derived and AGPL-3.0-only. The PDF reader is not in
this crate yet; the licence anticipates it. Whether `kopitiam-pdf` builds
for wasm32 has not been checked.

It does NOT depend on `kovan` or on any other AGPL crate: its data and layout
types come from `kovan-common` (GPL-3.0-only), which desktop kovan will also
use. Desktop kovan is expected to depend on this crate to embed the same UI,
so this crate must never depend on `kovan` or `dhoby-ghaut` (that would be a
cycle).

Code moved into kovan-common for it (2026-10-06)
------------------------------------------------

To build for wasm32, the pure data and layout modules this UI needs were moved
out of `kovan` (AGPL-3.0-only) into `kovan-common` (GPL-3.0-only):
`code_map` (model, layout, SVG), `call_graph` (model, module scanner),
`mindmap_view` (star layout, canvas arithmetic), `fuzzy` (the finders'
scorer), and `Point` / `Bounds` (now `kovan_common::geometry`). The
maintainer is the copyright holder of that code and directed on #743 that
the kovan family's shared schema live in kovan-common; `kovan` re-exports
each module under its old path. **CONFIRMED by the maintainer 2026-10-06:**
"Kovan common is GPLv3, it doesn't have mupdf there" -- kovan's AGPL comes
only from MuPDF (via kopitiam-pdf), which none of the moved code uses.

Ported pieces
-------------

`src/ui/camera.rs` ports the pan/zoom view, zoom buttons and canvas-size fix
of `dhoby_ghaut::web_demo` (same workspace, same copyright holder) rather
than depending on dhoby-ghaut, which depends on `kovan`.
